# 8. Agent architecture

Do not build an uncontrolled multi-agent swarm.

Use one orchestrator with bounded specialised services.

## Conversation orchestrator

Responsibilities:

* classify intent;
* collect missing context;
* call profile, plan, video or booking tools;
* maintain conversation state;
* generate concise responses;
* avoid repeating questions.

## Assessment service

Produces:

* primary goal;
* baseline;
* risk level;
* suitable starting protocol;
* missing information.

## Training-plan service

Uses deterministic rules and outputs a structured plan.

## Session-review service

Combines video observations with the current exercise criteria.

## Safety service

Runs before and after every recommendation.

## Professional-escalation service

Selects:

* remote trainer;
* local trainer;
* veterinary professional;
* urgent veterinary advice message where indicated.

## Commerce service

Handles:

* subscription entitlements;
* video credits;
* booking;
* referral attribution;
* disclosed affiliate recommendations.

A lightweight workflow engine or state machine is better than LangGraph for the basic user journey. LangGraph becomes useful only when you genuinely need resumable, branching, long-running agent workflows. Do not add it merely because the product uses an LLM.

