# 10. LLM-agnostic design

Create an internal provider contract.

```typescript
interface LanguageModelProvider {
  extractContext(input: ContextExtractionInput): Promise<StructuredContext>;
  generateUserMessage(input: MessageInput): Promise<string>;
  summarizeHistory(input: HistoryInput): Promise<HistorySummary>;
}

interface VideoLanguageProvider {
  analyzeClip(input: VideoAnalysisInput): Promise<SemanticVideoResult>;
}

interface LiveMultimodalProvider {
  createSession(input: LiveSessionConfig): Promise<LiveSession>;
}

interface ComputerVisionProvider {
  detectEntities(frames: FrameBatch): Promise<EntityTracks>;
  estimateHandlerPose(frames: FrameBatch): Promise<PoseSequence>;
  classifyEvents(input: TemporalFeatures): Promise<ObservedEvent[]>;
}
```

Store provider-independent results:

```text
raw provider response → adapter → canonical observation schema
```

Never store application logic in prompts that only work with one provider.

## Model routing

Use a policy:

```text
Simple chat classification
→ small/cheap language model

Plan explanation
→ normal fast model

Short uploaded video
→ Gemini Flash + deterministic CV

Low-confidence video
→ second-model verification or trainer review

Live session
→ local CV + Gemini Live

High-risk case
→ no autonomous advice; trainer/vet hand-off
```

