# 14. Real-time session design

## User experience

The owner opens a PWA link from WhatsApp.

The camera screen gives setup guidance:

```text
Place the phone 2–4 metres away
Keep the dog and your hands visible
Use landscape orientation
Avoid filming children or bystanders
Have rewards ready
```

During the exercise:

* local CV monitors dog, handler and visibility;
* microphone recognises verbal cue and marker words;
* Gemini Live handles conversation;
* the deterministic engine controls training instructions;
* unsafe signals pause the session;
* an approved trainer can join if booked.

## Real-time output types

### Immediate deterministic cues

* “Dog not visible.”
* “Move farther from the trigger.”
* “Leash has remained taut.”
* “You repeated the cue.”
* “Reward now.”
* “Pause.”
* “End the session.”

### Delayed interpretive feedback

* “Your timing improved during the last three repetitions.”
* “Your dog remained engaged at eight metres but disengaged at six.”
* “Next time, begin at eight metres.”

Avoid constantly talking. Real-time feedback should use:

* a soft tone;
* haptics;
* short sounds;
* one-sentence cues;
* configurable frequency.

