# 15. Development plan

## Phase 0 — protocol and safety foundation

Before coding advanced vision:

* recruit two to four qualified trainers or behaviour professionals;
* define launch problems;
* write 10–15 protocols;
* define risk and escalation rules;
* define observable-event taxonomy;
* define video annotation guidelines;
* define supported versus unsupported claims;
* establish trainer approval criteria.

Without this, the AI will only automate inconsistent advice.

## Phase 1 — WhatsApp assessment MVP

Build:

* WhatsApp Cloud API webhook;
* Supabase identity linking;
* dog profile;
* structured anamnesis;
* one goal;
* deterministic starter plan;
* daily check-ins;
* progress states;
* free assessment;
* subscription entitlements;
* basic trainer referral.

No video intelligence beyond manual or simple VLM review.

## Phase 2 — asynchronous video MVP

Build:

* secure upload;
* video-quality validation;
* person and dog detection;
* frame selection;
* audio transcription;
* Gemini video analysis;
* canonical observation schema;
* confidence grading;
* trainer-review queue;
* annotated timeline;
* user correction: “That observation is wrong.”

Support only three exercises initially:

* sit/down marker timing;
* loose-leash basics;
* calm engagement around low-level distractions.

## Phase 3 — precise temporal analysis

Add:

* handler pose;
* reward-event detection;
* cue and marker timing;
* leash-line detection;
* dog posture transitions;
* temporal event metrics;
* benchmark dataset;
* model evaluation dashboard.

## Phase 4 — live coaching beta

Build:

* LiveKit room;
* Gemini Live voice;
* local high-FPS CV;
* deterministic real-time cue engine;
* camera setup;
* trainer joining;
* consented recording;
* session summary.

Launch only for low-risk exercises.

## Phase 5 — trainer network and booking

Add:

* trainer portal;
* credential review;
* specialties and geography;
* Cal.com availability;
* native booking;
* Stripe Connect only when marketplace economics justify it;
* referral tracking;
* professional review workflows;
* trainer corrections feeding model evaluation.

## Phase 6 — canine-specific model improvement

Using consented, professionally labelled data:

* fine-tune dog posture model;
* breed/body-shape fairness testing;
* coat-colour and lighting evaluation;
* trigger and environment classifiers;
* active learning;
* disagreement review;
* model cards;
* controlled releases.

