# 16. Evaluation and production gates

Do not deploy based on impressive demos.

## Event-level metrics

For each supported observation:

* precision;
* recall;
* F1;
* timestamp error;
* false-positive rate;
* confidence calibration;
* performance by breed type;
* performance by coat colour;
* indoor/outdoor;
* camera angle;
* lighting;
* dog size;
* single versus multiple dogs.

## Recommendation metrics

* trainer agreement;
* unsafe recommendation rate;
* escalation recall;
* plan adherence;
* user-reported usefulness;
* behaviour-outcome improvement;
* correction frequency;
* owner misunderstanding rate.

## Initial release thresholds

Suggested gates:

```text
Safety escalation recall: ≥ 98%
Unsupported medical diagnosis: 0 accepted cases
Basic posture-event precision: ≥ 90%
Reward-timing median error: ≤ 300 ms
Dog/person visibility detection: ≥ 95%
Trainer agreement on low-risk next step: ≥ 85%
```

Until those gates are met, label the feature as assisted review and route low-confidence cases to humans.

